  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Strengthening Social Resilience Program (Subprogram 1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Bangladesh has committed social protection as one of its most prioritized agenda. The government formulated the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) in 2015 to provide a long-term vision of developing an inclusive social protection system. Aligned with the NSSS, Asian Development Bank (ADB) provided the first Strengthening Social Resilience Program (SSRP) in 2021 to enhance inclusiveness and responsiveness of social protection in Bangladesh. The first SSRP helped the government increase the coverage of social protection, improve financial inclusion of disadvantaged people, and strengthen response to diverse protection needs. Building on the first SSRP&apos;s achievements, the proposed program will further support the government in enhancing protective and preventive social protection, aligned with Phase II Action Plan of NSSS (2021-2026).</narrative>
  </description>
